star wars fans are reacting to the new  lego star wars dlc and halo fans aren't  too thrilled with the new battle rifle  changes  in celebration of may 4th aka star wars  day wb games have launched two new dlc  packs for lego star wars the skywalker  saga one of the packs the mandalorian  season 2 features characters like ahsoka  boba fett and moff gideon the other pack  star wars the bad batch features  characters like hunter wrecker tech  crosshair and echo players can purchase  these new packs separately or they can  grab the character collection pack which  includes mando season 1 solo a star wars  story rogue one and more fans of the  game reacted to the new dlc trailer and  expressed some interest in more than  just new characters in the youtube  comments users said things like quote  now what i need are story dlcs i play  through clone wars and the mandalorian  for example dlcs with new story missions  will be incredible over on reddit users  seem to have a similar opinion and said  things like quote those are just  characters no new missions or planets a  bit of a letdown yeah i feel like  initial marketing indicated at a minimum  rogue one and solo would get story  content so overall it seems like fans  have their fingers crossed for both  clone wars and story missions in some  form or another hit the comments of this  video and let me know what you're hoping  for personally i was hoping for the game  to go on sale today but i guess it's too  soon for that tomorrow makes a full  month since the game actually released  not to mention the game has also sold  incredibly well becoming the biggest  launch in the history of the lego series  selling through 3.2 million units over  its first two weeks another game that  features wars in space is halo and a  ranked only melee buff for the battle  rifle in halo infinite season 2 has not  gone over very well with fans the buff  for the battle rifles melee in the  ranked playlist essentially keeps the  weapon performing as it was in season 1  following the otherwise universal 10  melee damage reduction introduced as a  part of season 2. the patch notes state  the battle rifle's melee damage was kept  intact and ranked in order to preserve  the battle rifle's two burst beatdown  after the global melee reduction it's  also important to note that all players  start with a battle rifle in ranked fans  by and large don't seem to be thrilled  with the battle rifle change having a  weapon that performs differently and  ranked as opposed to other playlists  players on the halo infinite subreddit  argue that having a weapon that performs  differently in ranked as opposed to all  other playlists makes the game more  confusing and punishing for players who  jump in between different playlists  frequently the move seems to cater to  the game's more competitive community  who would be upset if the battle rifle  receives significant changes but in the  process upset the game's more casual  audience many fans are wondering why 343  didn't simply add the melee damage buff  to the battle rifle in social playlists  as well and in other online shooter news  apex legends might start releasing  characters slower in a new interview the  game's senior character designer devin  maguire explained that while apex  legends is more about movement and  firearms than legend abilities those  abilities can still unbalance the game  as it becomes more difficult to create  characters who are unique without being  too overpowered or niche with each  passing season maguire explained that  the game may reach a breaking point  where adding a new legend every season  may become detrimental to the game  itself saying quote whether or not that  pattern continues is an ongoing  discussion and it might not be changed  but we don't want to saturate the pool  of legends so what do you think about  this would you mind if they slowed down  the release of legends and what other  games do you think should slow down with  the release of characters
 

